# Release-archive contents (`git archive`, used by scripts/package-windows.mjs).
#
# This repository was scaffolded inside the Grok App Builder sandbox and still
# carries that sandbox's material: the agent contract (AGENTS.md, which points
# at AGENTS.project.md), the skill trees, references and status files under
# .grok/, the dated handoffs, the audit reports under artifacts/, and the
# sandbox's own startup.sh. That material stays in the source repository as
# history, but it is not the product -- none of it belongs in the Windows ZIP a
# publisher downloads. `export-ignore` is read by `git archive`, so the
# exclusions are what actually keeps the scaffold out of the release; see
# scripts/release-archive-contents.test.mjs.
#
# Each directory needs both lines. In .gitattributes a directory pattern does
# not recurse into the directory's contents, and a contents-only pattern
# (`dir/**`) still leaves `git archive --format=tar` emitting the bare `dir/`
# entry.
.grok export-ignore
.grok/** export-ignore
artifacts export-ignore
artifacts/** export-ignore
AGENTS.md export-ignore
AGENTS.project.md export-ignore
# The dated and session handoffs only. HANDOFF-NEXT-AGENT.md is the current
# takeover handoff and is linked from live documentation (SELF-HOSTING.md,
# docs/dark-desk.md, docs/releases/), so it ships. docs/archive/HANDOFF-0.4.3.md
# is dated product history and ships too -- hence the root anchor on all three.
/HANDOFF-2026-*.md export-ignore
/HANDOFF-SESSION-*.md export-ignore
/HANDOFF-BUILD-LIST.md export-ignore
startup.sh export-ignore
